<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This 10-day Silk Road group tour takes you through the three legendary provinces of Xinjiang, Gansu, and Qinghai. From the bustling markets of Urumqi and the ancient ruins of Turpan, to the awe-inspiring Mogao Caves in Dunhuang, the mighty Jiayuguan Fortress, the rainbow-colored Zhangye Danxia, and the mirror-like Chaka Salt Lake — every day unveils a new chapter of the ancient Silk Road. Travel with a small group (max 16), stay in comfortable 4-star hotels, and enjoy the expertise of our English-speaking guides.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Discover Urumqi's Xinjiang Museum and Hongshan Park</li><li>Explore ancient Jiaohe Ruins and the Karez irrigation system in Turpan</li>
      <li>Visit the UNESCO Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li><li>Camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes & Crescent Moon Spring</li>
      <li>Walk the Jiayuguan Fortress — the western end of the Great Wall</li><li>Rainbow Mountains at Zhangye Danxia at sunset</li>
      <li>Photograph Chaka Salt Lake — the "Mirror of the Sky"</li><li>Tibetan culture experience in Xining</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Urumqi</h4><p>Arrive at Urumqi Diwopu International Airport. Your guide will meet you and transfer to your hotel. Afternoon visit to the Xinjiang Regional Museum to see the famous Tarim mummies. Evening at Hongshan Park for panoramic views of Urumqi against the Tianshan Mountains.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi → Turpan — Jiaohe Ruins & Karez System</h4><p>Drive to Turpan (3 hours), the second-lowest depression on Earth. Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins, a 2,000-year-old city carved from raw earth. Discover the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system, a Silk Road engineering marvel that still waters the oasis today.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan — Flaming Mountains & Grape Valley → High-speed Train to Dunhuang</h4><p>Morning visit to the Flaming Mountains, glowing red under the desert sun. Stroll through Grape Valley, a lush oasis famous for its sweet Turpan grapes. Afternoon high-speed train to Dunhuang (approx. 4 hours), crossing the vast Gobi landscape.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full UNESCO day. Morning at the Mogao Caves (8 caves included), a millennium of Buddhist art carved into the cliffs. Afternoon camel ride and sand surfing at the Singing Sand Dunes. Optional sunset at Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive to Jiayuguan (5 hours) through the Gobi Desert. Visit the Jiayuguan Fortress, the western end of the Great Wall of China, standing majestically where the desert meets the mountains.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Zhangye — Danxia at Sunset</h4><p>Morning visit to the Overhanging Great Wall. Drive to Zhangye (2.5 hours). Late afternoon at Zhangye Danxia — the famous rainbow-colored rock formations, best photographed at sunset when the colors blaze across the landscape.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Zhangye 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye Giant Buddha Temple → High-speed Train to Xining</h4><p>Morning at the Giant Buddha Temple, home to Asia's largest reclining Buddha. High-speed train to Xining (approx. 3 hours), capital of Qinghai province. Evening stroll through the Muslim quarter and visit Dongguan Mosque.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xining — Chaka Salt Lake & Kumbum Monastery</h4><p>Drive to Chaka Salt Lake (4 hours), the "Mirror of the Sky." Walk on the salt flats and capture stunning reflection photos. Visit Kumbum Monastery (Ta'er Si) on the return journey, one of the most important Tibetan Buddhist monasteries outside Tibet.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xining — Free Day & Tibetan Culture</h4><p>A relaxed day in Xining. Explore the city's Tibetan culture at the Qinghai Tibetan Medicine Museum, browse local markets for handicrafts, or simply enjoy the highland atmosphere. Optional evening food tour through Xining's vibrant night market.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Xining</h4><p>Free time until your airport transfer. Your 10-day Silk Road adventure concludes. 再见!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>9 nights 4-star hotel accommodation (twin-share)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>English-speaking guide throughout</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All high-speed train tickets (Turpan→Dunhuang, Zhangye→Xining)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Private air-conditioned vehicle & driver</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Meals as indicated (B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All entrance fees & listed activities</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Airport transfers on arrival & departure</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Travel insurance (China domestic)</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What's Excluded</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>International flights to/from China</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Chinese visa fees</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Personal expenses & tips</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Single room supplement ($380)</p></div>
    </div>

